            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether, after the divorce but before the policy owner died, the owner paid premiums."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1a8416c0d792-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Gorsuch asked what would happen if the policy did not go to its contingent beneficiaries."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan questioned whether the timing of the divorce relative to the statute mattered."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked whether it is a fair assumption that most people do not want a former spouse enriched after divorce."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg further asked whether it is reasonable for a legislature to assume that most people would rather leave life\u2011insurance proceeds to their children than to a divorced spouse."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1a8416c0d792-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 69,
              "start": 69
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Gorsuch referenced Justice Marshall\u2019s view that marriage contracts are not within the Contracts Clause\u2019s cognizance and asked whether life\u2011insurance policies are."
      }
    ],
