            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Oral argument in this case was heard by the Supreme Court on Monday, March 19, 2018 at 10:05\u202fa.m."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1a8416c0d792-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, the case presents the question whether applying a revocation\u2011on\u2011divorce statute to a life\u2011insurance policy that was purchased before the statute\u2019s enactment violates the Contracts Clause."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1a8416c0d792-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Historically, revocation\u2011on\u2011divorce statutes were intended to align the law of life\u2011insurance policies with the law of wills."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0013"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Beneficiary designations are determined in accordance with the terms of the contract."
      }
    ],
